From 8f2019736f957847b4afee183b050a479226b64e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:23:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/resample_audio: do not report success when the
 reallocation fails

When the destination buffer has to grow and av_samples_alloc() fails,
the loop is left with break. The code after the loop then overwrites
the error code, prints "Resampling succeeded" and the program returns
0 although the output is truncated.

Jump to the cleanup code instead, like the other error paths do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/resample_audio.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/resample_audio.c b/doc/examples/resample_audio.c
index 4b33af7..e60a0a3 100644
--- a/doc/examples/resample_audio.c
+++ b/doc/examples/resample_audio.c
@@ -176,8 +176,10 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
             av_freep(&dst_data[0]);
             ret = av_samples_alloc(dst_data, &dst_linesize, dst_nb_channels,
                                    dst_nb_samples, dst_sample_fmt, 1);
-            if (ret < 0)
-                break;
+            if (ret < 0) {
+                fprintf(stderr, "Could not allocate destination samples\n");
+                goto end;
+            }
             max_dst_nb_samples = dst_nb_samples;
         }
 
